{
  "summary": "Hardens node `interfaces::Chain` method implementations against crashes caused by invalid arguments or client errors over IPC. It substitutes assertions and null pointer dereferences with bounds checking and error returns, catches `ipc::Exception` in notification handlers to prevent validation scheduler thread terminations, and fixes a logic bug in `findAncestorByHash`.",
  "problem": "`interfaces::Chain` was originally written under the assumption of well-behaved in-process callers like the internal wallet. When exposed over multiprocess IPC (as in #29409), omitted fields or invalid parameters cause the node to assert or dereference null, an error returned by an IPC notification handler terminates the validation scheduler thread, and `findAncestorByHash` erroneously returns true when a descendant block is unknown (#36472).",
  "evidence": [
    "Issue #36472 demonstrates that `findAncestorByHash` returns true when ancestor_hash is known but block_hash is unknown.",
    "PR description notes that reviewers of multiprocess PR #29409 (zaidmstrr, willcl-ark, xyzconstant) identified that out-of-bounds `getBlockHash` asserts, null transaction arguments cause null dereferences, and uncaught notification IPC exceptions terminate the node."
  ],
