      "#29409"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "The diff was not provided in the input, but commit messages indicate changes are localized to `src/node/interfaces.cpp` and unit tests in `src/test/interfaces_tests.cpp` across three commits.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "This PR hardens Bitcoin Core's Chain interface implementations against crashes from invalid inputs and catches IPC exceptions originating from notification handlers. Currently, Chain methods assume well-behaved in-process C++ callers, asserting or dereferencing null pointers on invalid inputs and permitting uncaught exceptions on the validation scheduler thread, which crashes the node when exposed to IPC clients. It also fixes an active bug (issue 36472) where findAncestorByHash reports success for unknown descendant blocks. While standalone, this change primarily safeguards the node for multiprocess IPC support in PR 29409.",
